 {"id":"INSTALL-OFF-BY-ONE-2026-10-13","title":"[P2] INSTALL verified on ephemeral bunker (bunker-mvp; las-01/02/03/04 all offline): clone+build 84s -> seed 23s (2638/2736/11698) -> serve health ok -> discover fallback proven on fresh install","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"task","created_by":"off-by-one-dogfood","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:10:00Z","reasoning":"Fresh Debian user on bunker-mvp (agent oby-df2026, ttl 2h; las-bunker-01/02/03/04 offline on tailscale, bunker-mvp the only answering host). Public https clone of HEAD bc95faf, make build 84s rc=0, ./off-by-one --version = off-by-one bc95faf, seed 23s rc=0 (files=2638 classes=2638 answers=2736/1530 skipped edges=11698), serve on :8901 health ok, stats 2638/2736 verified=2736, discover {class=so-nil-pointer-deref, version=1.26.1} -> found:true (re-proves DF-36's fallback on a fresh machine + fresh seed, commit d18586d6 in the build). Smoke quirk (tester error, not product): seed honors OFF_BY_ONE_DB but a -db flag server started from a different CWD/db reads an empty store - use the env var consistently. Agent destroyed, list clean after 90s recheck (a sibling agent oby-df1013 spawned by another lane is present, not ours). bunker exec stream deadlines again: stage scripts via bunker cp (direct scp path oby-df2026:$HOME/x fails, relative target works), run under $HOME (tmp not trusted)."}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-42","title":"[P1] Explore tree: expanding a version node renders an EMPTY children div \u2014 no answer leaves, dead end at the deepest drill-down level","status":"complete","priority":"P1","created_by":"dogfood-tick-2026-10-13-0537","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:20:00Z","reasoning":"Real-use drive of the web UI Explore view (surface never exercised in 18 prior dogfood runs). Drilling class\u2192env\u2192lang\u2192version works, but clicking the version node ('any') toggles the icon to \u25bc and leaves .tree-children EMPTY \u2014 the answer leaf (renderAnswerLeaf) never renders, so a user can never reach an answer through the tree (the advertised path: 'problem class \u2192 environment \u2192 language \u2192 version \u2192 answer'). Root cause found by reading the served JS: explore.js toggleSubNode calls renderVersionChildren(children, classTitle, parentValue, answers) (4 args) but the function is declared function renderVersionChildren(container, answers) (2 args) \u2014 the answers array lands in the parentValue parameter and answers is undefined; forEach on undefined throws inside the handler, silently swallowed. Evidence: live DOM .tree-node.tree-version .tree-children innerHTML === '' after expand; grep of /js/explore.js confirms both the 4-arg call site and the 2-arg signature (arity_bug: true); the same file's renderEnvChildren/renderLangChildren have 4-arg signatures and work. Repro: open /, Explore tab, expand go-vet-copylocks-value-receiver-on-sync-mutex-20261013 \u2192 linux \u2192 go \u2192 any. Fix direction: align the version-level call to renderVersionChildren(children, answers) (or give renderVersionChildren the same 4-arg shape and ignore the middle params). Add a render test that expands every level of the tree and asserts .tree-answer nodes exist (a payload-shape/render test would have caught this: the API payload is correct \u2014 /api/v1/taxonomy carries the answers).","found_by":"dogfood 2026-10-13 (UI-surface tick)"}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-43","title":"[P2] Submit view renders HTTP 409 'deduplicated' \u2014 an API success shape \u2014 as 'Submission failed (HTTP 409)' with no submission_id and no link to the existing answer","status":"complete","priority":"P2","created_by":"dogfood-tick-2026-10-13-0537","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:20:00Z","reasoning":"Real-use drive of the web UI Submit view (surface never exercised in 18 prior runs). Submitting df-ui-golang-http-client-timeout-retry-budget-20261013 through the form succeeded \u2014 the server returned 409 with the documented dedup contract body {submission_id:'sub_e3894e', status:'deduplicated', position:1, estimated_time:''} (the API treats dedup as a success: the submission EXISTS). The UI's submit.js keys only on HTTP status and renders 'Submission failed (HTTP 409)', leaves the form values intact, and shows nothing else \u2014 a real user reads 'failed' for a submission that actually landed in the queue, and gets no pointer to the existing entry. Reproduced live (response captured via fetch wrapper: 409 /api/v1/problems/submit {submission_id:sub_e3894e,...status:deduplicated}). Fix direction: in the submit handler, treat 409 + status==='deduplicated' as success \u2014 show 'Already queued (sub_e3894e), position 1' and clear/disable the form; keep 'Submission failed' for 4xx bodies that carry an error field. This is the UI twin of DF-OFF-BY-ONE-37 (CLI dedup 409 with empty id) \u2014 same contract, second surface, so file UI-side handling separately rather than reopening 37.","found_by":"dogfood 2026-10-13 (UI-surface tick)"}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-44","title":"[P2] Chat panel flaps: 11 'Connected to Off-by-One AI Agent' system banners accumulated in ~3 minutes (client-side reconnect loop) and the user's sent message never renders in the transcript","status":"complete","priority":"P2","created_by":"dogfood-tick-2026-10-13-0537","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:20:00Z","reasoning":"Real-use drive of the AI chat sidebar (web UI surface never exercised in 18 prior runs). Observed: chat-body accumulated 9 'Connected\u2026' system banners within ~2 min of page load (11 after 3 min), each new connection appending a fresh banner instead of replacing the status line; input flips between 'Reconnecting\u2026' and 'Ask the agent\u2026'. Server side is NOT the bottleneck \u2014 a raw socket probe (python /tmp/oby-ws-probe.py pattern, hand-rolled WS handshake) completed the 101 upgrade in 0.00s and received exactly ONE banner frame, so the flapping is the client: the page's own WS reconnects in a loop (possibly duplicate initView_chat invocations or a ping/pong timer the client treats as close). Separately, sending 'How do I fix go vet copylocks?' via the input produced NO transcript entry for the user message (grep of chat-body: false) and no agent reply within 25s \u2014 the send path appears to require a connected socket and silently drops otherwise. Fix direction: (a) appendMessage('system', \u2026) for the connect banner should replace the existing status banner, not append; (b) find and fix the client reconnect trigger (log ws.onclose codes); (c) echo the user's own message into the transcript on send regardless of socket state, with a 'sending\u2026' marker. Repro: open /, watch chat sidebar 3 min; send a message right after a 'Reconnecting\u2026' phase.","found_by":"dogfood 2026-10-13 (UI-surface tick)"}
